<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Marines</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1664">1664</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal Marines are the amphibious infantry of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a>, whose origins go back to a regiment raised for sea service in 1664. They have fought in most British wars, from the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a> in 1704 to the Falklands War. In January 1964 Royal Marine commandos were called in by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a> to disarm the mutinous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanganyika-rifles">Tanganyika Rifles</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-marines.jpg" alt="Royal Marines" width="320" height="504" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RoyalMarineBadge.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
